From 1d33b4a99e7a6e080fc30da7d370badfad98e50e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v1): roll back failed frontend request submissions

Base: candidate-38 patch head 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4; the affected host code is unchanged in candidate-39.

Registering locally before the async engine send is necessary for admission accounting, but a cancelled or failed send can leave that request retained forever: generate has not yet received its queue handle. Roll back the complete submission using the original internal queue ID, including partially submitted sampling children, and preserve the original failure if the abort notification also fails.

Quality: healthy requests, decoding, token selection, context limits and GPU work are unchanged. Cleanup follows existing abort semantics and cannot abort an unrelated request that reuses the external ID.

Tests: CPU regressions cover blocked-send cancellation through generate, failed sends, sampled children, repeated external IDs, abort-send failure and ordinary successful completion. Target validation is on Spaceport.

Upstream status: local, not submitted.
